<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melisende Psalter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1135</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Melisende <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-psalms">Psalter</a> is an illuminated psalter made in the scriptorium of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre">Church of the Holy Sepulchre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> around 1131–1143, probably for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melisende-queen-of-jerusalem">Queen Melisende</a>. Its miniatures and carved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> covers combine Byzantine, Western European and Eastern Christian styles, and it is one of the finest surviving works of crusader art. It is now in the British Library in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melisende-psalter.jpg" alt="Melisende Psalter" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Creator:Basilius · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Presentation_of_Christ_in_the_Temple_-_Psalter_of_Queen_Melisende_(1131-1143),_f.3_-_BL_Egerton_MS_1139.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
